{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Hotkeys ships devtools for debugging and monitoring your registered hotkeys in real time, as a panel inside the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/devtools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Devtools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" multi-panel UI."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Hotkeys devtools exports are no-ops outside development mode. The Angular and Svelte setup examples below also guard the TanStack Devtools dock so it does not mount in production. To debug a production build, use the explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/production"},{"type":"text","value":" Hotkeys exports."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"features","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Features"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Hotkeys devtools panel lets you:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"View all currently registered hotkeys with their options and status"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See which keys are held down in real time"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trigger hotkey callbacks for testing, without pressing the keys"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inspect individual registrations, including their target, event type, and conflict behavior"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install the devtools packages for your framework:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"angular","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requires Angular 21 or newer."}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/angular-devtools @tanstack/angular-hotkeys-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"svelte","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requires Svelte 5.25 or newer within version 5."}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/svelte-devtools @tanstack/svelte-hotkeys-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/react-devtools @tanstack/react-hotkeys-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"preact","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preact"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/preact-devtools @tanstack/preact-hotkeys-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"solid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/solid-devtools @tanstack/solid-hotkeys-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/vue-hotkeys-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alpine, Ember, Lit, and Octane do not currently ship dedicated Hotkeys devtools adapters."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setup"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"angular-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add the plugin through the official "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provideTanStackDevtools"},{"type":"text","value":" provider in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"app.config.ts"},{"type":"text","value":". The provider creates the dock; you do not need to add a component to your template."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { isDevMode } from '@angular/core'\nimport { provideTanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/angular-devtools/provider'\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys-devtools'\nimport type { ApplicationConfig } from '@angular/core'\n\nexport const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n  providers: [\n    ...(isDevMode()\n      ? [\n          provideTanStackDevtools(() => ({\n            plugins: [hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()],\n          })),\n        ]\n      : []),\n  ],\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep your existing application providers alongside this provider."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"svelte-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add the dock once in your root component. This example uses Vite's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"import.meta.env.DEV"},{"type":"text","value":" flag to keep the dock out of production builds."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys-devtools'\n</script>\n\n{#if import.meta.env.DEV}\n  <TanStackDevtools plugins={[hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n{/if}","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In SvelteKit, you can use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dev"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$app/environment"},{"type":"text","value":" as the condition instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"react-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React setup"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/react-devtools'\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return <TanStackDevtools plugins={[hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"preact-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preact setup"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/preact-devtools'\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nexport function App() {\n  return <TanStackDevtools plugins={[hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"solid-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid setup"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/solid-devtools'\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nexport function App() {\n  return <TanStackDevtools plugins={[hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vue-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue setup"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { HotkeysDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys-devtools'\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <AppContent />\n  <HotkeysDevtoolsPanel />\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For Angular, Svelte, React, Preact, and Solid, the Hotkeys panel appears alongside any other TanStack devtools plugins you have installed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"standalone-panel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standalone panel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React, Preact, and Solid also export "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeysDevtoolsPanel"},{"type":"text","value":" for rendering without the TanStack Devtools dock:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { HotkeysDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/react-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nfunction DebugPanel() {\n  return <HotkeysDevtoolsPanel />\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the corresponding "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/preact-hotkeys-devtools"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/solid-hotkeys-devtools"},{"type":"text","value":" import for those frameworks. The panel and no-op component also accept an omitted props argument during rendering. Both props are optional: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'dark'"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"devtoolsOpen"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":". Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme=\"light\""},{"type":"text","value":" to select the light theme. When using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()"},{"type":"text","value":", the dock supplies these props and its values take precedence over the standalone defaults."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte also exports a standalone component:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { HotkeysDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys-devtools'\n</script>\n\n<HotkeysDevtoolsPanel theme=\"light\" />","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeysDevtoolsPanel"},{"type":"text","value":" is a render factory for the official dock. To mount it in your own host element, call the factory and keep its returned cleanup function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { HotkeysDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nexport function mountHotkeysPanel(host: HTMLElement) {\n  const render = HotkeysDevtoolsPanel()\n  return render?.(() => ({ theme: 'light' }), host)\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call the returned cleanup function when the host is destroyed. The factory returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" outside development mode. Both Angular and Svelte use the same standalone defaults as React: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme: 'dark'"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"devtoolsOpen: true"},{"type":"text","value":". Values supplied by the dock take precedence over these defaults."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"production-builds","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production builds"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In production builds, the framework devtools adapters return no-op implementations, so they don't affect your bundle's behavior."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React also exposes a production import for when you explicitly want the plugin in production:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-hotkeys-devtools/production'","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular and Svelte also provide explicit production exports:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys-devtools/production'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"import { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys-devtools/production'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remove the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isDevMode()"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"import.meta.env.DEV"},{"type":"text","value":" guard from the corresponding setup example when you intentionally want the dock in production. These entry points also export the active "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeysDevtoolsPanel"},{"type":"text","value":" for standalone use."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"features","text":"Features","level":2},{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"angular","text":"Angular","level":3},{"id":"svelte","text":"Svelte","level":3},{"id":"react","text":"React","level":3},{"id":"preact","text":"Preact","level":3},{"id":"solid","text":"Solid","level":3},{"id":"vue","text":"Vue","level":3},{"id":"setup","text":"Setup","level":2},{"id":"angular-setup","text":"Angular setup","level":3},{"id":"svelte-setup","text":"Svelte setup","level":3},{"id":"react-setup","text":"React setup","level":3},{"id":"preact-setup","text":"Preact setup","level":3},{"id":"solid-setup","text":"Solid setup","level":3},{"id":"vue-setup","text":"Vue setup","level":3},{"id":"standalone-panel","text":"Standalone panel","level":3},{"id":"production-builds","text":"Production builds","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Hotkeys ships devtools for debugging and monitoring your registered hotkeys in real time, as a panel inside the [TanStack Devtools](https://tanstack.com/devtools) multi-panel UI.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> The Hotkeys devtools exports are no-ops outside development mode. The Angular and Svelte setup examples below also guard the TanStack Devtools dock so it does not mount in production. To debug a production build, use the explicit `/production` Hotkeys exports.\n\n## Features\n\nThe Hotkeys devtools panel lets you:\n\n- View all currently registered hotkeys with their options and status\n- See which keys are held down in real time\n- Trigger hotkey callbacks for testing, without pressing the keys\n- Inspect individual registrations, including their target, event type, and conflict behavior\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall the devtools packages for your framework:\n\n### Angular\n\nRequires Angular 21 or newer.\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/angular-devtools @tanstack/angular-hotkeys-devtools\n```\n\n### Svelte\n\nRequires Svelte 5.25 or newer within version 5.\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/svelte-devtools @tanstack/svelte-hotkeys-devtools\n```\n\n### React\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/react-devtools @tanstack/react-hotkeys-devtools\n```\n\n### Preact\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/preact-devtools @tanstack/preact-hotkeys-devtools\n```\n\n### Solid\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/solid-devtools @tanstack/solid-hotkeys-devtools\n```\n\n### Vue\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/vue-hotkeys-devtools\n```\n\nAlpine, Ember, Lit, and Octane do not currently ship dedicated Hotkeys devtools adapters.\n\n## Setup\n\n### Angular setup\n\nAdd the plugin through the official `provideTanStackDevtools` provider in `app.config.ts`. The provider creates the dock; you do not need to add a component to your template.\n\n```ts\nimport { isDevMode } from '@angular/core'\nimport { provideTanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/angular-devtools/provider'\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys-devtools'\nimport type { ApplicationConfig } from '@angular/core'\n\nexport const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n  providers: [\n    ...(isDevMode()\n      ? [\n          provideTanStackDevtools(() => ({\n            plugins: [hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()],\n          })),\n        ]\n      : []),\n  ],\n}\n```\n\nKeep your existing application providers alongside this provider.\n\n### Svelte setup\n\nAdd the dock once in your root component. This example uses Vite's `import.meta.env.DEV` flag to keep the dock out of production builds.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys-devtools'\n</script>\n\n{#if import.meta.env.DEV}\n  <TanStackDevtools plugins={[hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n{/if}\n```\n\nIn SvelteKit, you can use `dev` from `$app/environment` as the condition instead.\n\n### React setup\n\n```tsx\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/react-devtools'\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return <TanStackDevtools plugins={[hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n}\n```\n\n### Preact setup\n\n```tsx\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/preact-devtools'\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nexport function App() {\n  return <TanStackDevtools plugins={[hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n}\n```\n\n### Solid setup\n\n```tsx\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/solid-devtools'\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nexport function App() {\n  return <TanStackDevtools plugins={[hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n}\n```\n\n### Vue setup\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { HotkeysDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys-devtools'\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <AppContent />\n  <HotkeysDevtoolsPanel />\n</template>\n```\n\nFor Angular, Svelte, React, Preact, and Solid, the Hotkeys panel appears alongside any other TanStack devtools plugins you have installed.\n\n### Standalone panel\n\nReact, Preact, and Solid also export `HotkeysDevtoolsPanel` for rendering without the TanStack Devtools dock:\n\n```tsx\nimport { HotkeysDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/react-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nfunction DebugPanel() {\n  return <HotkeysDevtoolsPanel />\n}\n```\n\nUse the corresponding `@tanstack/preact-hotkeys-devtools` or `@tanstack/solid-hotkeys-devtools` import for those frameworks. The panel and no-op component also accept an omitted props argument during rendering. Both props are optional: `theme` defaults to `'dark'` and `devtoolsOpen` defaults to `true`. Pass `theme=\"light\"` to select the light theme. When using `hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()`, the dock supplies these props and its values take precedence over the standalone defaults.\n\nSvelte also exports a standalone component:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { HotkeysDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys-devtools'\n</script>\n\n<HotkeysDevtoolsPanel theme=\"light\" />\n```\n\nAngular's `HotkeysDevtoolsPanel` is a render factory for the official dock. To mount it in your own host element, call the factory and keep its returned cleanup function:\n\n```ts\nimport { HotkeysDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nexport function mountHotkeysPanel(host: HTMLElement) {\n  const render = HotkeysDevtoolsPanel()\n  return render?.(() => ({ theme: 'light' }), host)\n}\n```\n\nCall the returned cleanup function when the host is destroyed. The factory returns `null` outside development mode. Both Angular and Svelte use the same standalone defaults as React: `theme: 'dark'` and `devtoolsOpen: true`. Values supplied by the dock take precedence over these defaults.\n\n## Production builds\n\nIn production builds, the framework devtools adapters return no-op implementations, so they don't affect your bundle's behavior.\n\nReact also exposes a production import for when you explicitly want the plugin in production:\n\n```tsx\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-hotkeys-devtools/production'\n```\n\nAngular and Svelte also provide explicit production exports:\n\n```ts\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys-devtools/production'\n```\n\n```ts\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys-devtools/production'\n```\n\nRemove the `isDevMode()` or `import.meta.env.DEV` guard from the corresponding setup example when you intentionally want the dock in production. These entry points also export the active `HotkeysDevtoolsPanel` for standalone use.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Devtools\nid: devtools\n---\n\nTanStack Hotkeys ships devtools for debugging and monitoring your registered hotkeys in real time, as a panel inside the [TanStack Devtools](https://tanstack.com/devtools) multi-panel UI.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> The Hotkeys devtools exports are no-ops outside development mode. The Angular and Svelte setup examples below also guard the TanStack Devtools dock so it does not mount in production. To debug a production build, use the explicit `/production` Hotkeys exports.\n\n## Features\n\nThe Hotkeys devtools panel lets you:\n\n- View all currently registered hotkeys with their options and status\n- See which keys are held down in real time\n- Trigger hotkey callbacks for testing, without pressing the keys\n- Inspect individual registrations, including their target, event type, and conflict behavior\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall the devtools packages for your framework:\n\n### Angular\n\nRequires Angular 21 or newer.\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/angular-devtools @tanstack/angular-hotkeys-devtools\n```\n\n### Svelte\n\nRequires Svelte 5.25 or newer within version 5.\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/svelte-devtools @tanstack/svelte-hotkeys-devtools\n```\n\n### React\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/react-devtools @tanstack/react-hotkeys-devtools\n```\n\n### Preact\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/preact-devtools @tanstack/preact-hotkeys-devtools\n```\n\n### Solid\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/solid-devtools @tanstack/solid-hotkeys-devtools\n```\n\n### Vue\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/vue-hotkeys-devtools\n```\n\nAlpine, Ember, Lit, and Octane do not currently ship dedicated Hotkeys devtools adapters.\n\n## Setup\n\n### Angular setup\n\nAdd the plugin through the official `provideTanStackDevtools` provider in `app.config.ts`. The provider creates the dock; you do not need to add a component to your template.\n\n```ts\nimport { isDevMode } from '@angular/core'\nimport { provideTanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/angular-devtools/provider'\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys-devtools'\nimport type { ApplicationConfig } from '@angular/core'\n\nexport const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n  providers: [\n    ...(isDevMode()\n      ? [\n          provideTanStackDevtools(() => ({\n            plugins: [hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()],\n          })),\n        ]\n      : []),\n  ],\n}\n```\n\nKeep your existing application providers alongside this provider.\n\n### Svelte setup\n\nAdd the dock once in your root component. This example uses Vite's `import.meta.env.DEV` flag to keep the dock out of production builds.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys-devtools'\n</script>\n\n{#if import.meta.env.DEV}\n  <TanStackDevtools plugins={[hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n{/if}\n```\n\nIn SvelteKit, you can use `dev` from `$app/environment` as the condition instead.\n\n### React setup\n\n```tsx\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/react-devtools'\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return <TanStackDevtools plugins={[hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n}\n```\n\n### Preact setup\n\n```tsx\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/preact-devtools'\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nexport function App() {\n  return <TanStackDevtools plugins={[hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n}\n```\n\n### Solid setup\n\n```tsx\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/solid-devtools'\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nexport function App() {\n  return <TanStackDevtools plugins={[hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n}\n```\n\n### Vue setup\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { HotkeysDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys-devtools'\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <AppContent />\n  <HotkeysDevtoolsPanel />\n</template>\n```\n\nFor Angular, Svelte, React, Preact, and Solid, the Hotkeys panel appears alongside any other TanStack devtools plugins you have installed.\n\n### Standalone panel\n\nReact, Preact, and Solid also export `HotkeysDevtoolsPanel` for rendering without the TanStack Devtools dock:\n\n```tsx\nimport { HotkeysDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/react-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nfunction DebugPanel() {\n  return <HotkeysDevtoolsPanel />\n}\n```\n\nUse the corresponding `@tanstack/preact-hotkeys-devtools` or `@tanstack/solid-hotkeys-devtools` import for those frameworks. The panel and no-op component also accept an omitted props argument during rendering. Both props are optional: `theme` defaults to `'dark'` and `devtoolsOpen` defaults to `true`. Pass `theme=\"light\"` to select the light theme. When using `hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin()`, the dock supplies these props and its values take precedence over the standalone defaults.\n\nSvelte also exports a standalone component:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { HotkeysDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys-devtools'\n</script>\n\n<HotkeysDevtoolsPanel theme=\"light\" />\n```\n\nAngular's `HotkeysDevtoolsPanel` is a render factory for the official dock. To mount it in your own host element, call the factory and keep its returned cleanup function:\n\n```ts\nimport { HotkeysDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys-devtools'\n\nexport function mountHotkeysPanel(host: HTMLElement) {\n  const render = HotkeysDevtoolsPanel()\n  return render?.(() => ({ theme: 'light' }), host)\n}\n```\n\nCall the returned cleanup function when the host is destroyed. The factory returns `null` outside development mode. Both Angular and Svelte use the same standalone defaults as React: `theme: 'dark'` and `devtoolsOpen: true`. Values supplied by the dock take precedence over these defaults.\n\n## Production builds\n\nIn production builds, the framework devtools adapters return no-op implementations, so they don't affect your bundle's behavior.\n\nReact also exposes a production import for when you explicitly want the plugin in production:\n\n```tsx\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-hotkeys-devtools/production'\n```\n\nAngular and Svelte also provide explicit production exports:\n\n```ts\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys-devtools/production'\n```\n\n```ts\nimport { hotkeysDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys-devtools/production'\n```\n\nRemove the `isDevMode()` or `import.meta.env.DEV` guard from the corresponding setup example when you intentionally want the dock in production. These entry points also export the active `HotkeysDevtoolsPanel` for standalone use.\n"}
